lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "934f0c8fdcfddd95c2757336b5e70a6ced50964478ae4775dd3ae1f874e53db1" ;
    lgo:text """(1) For the consumer, the following contractual provisions within the meaning of § 879 ABGB are in any event not binding, under which
1. the trader reserves an unreasonably long or insufficiently specific period during which he may accept or reject a contractual offer of the consumer or during which the consumer is bound to the contract;
2. particular conduct of the consumer is treated as the making or non-making of a declaration, unless the consumer is specifically advised at the beginning of the period provided for this purpose of the significance of his conduct and has a reasonable period to make an express declaration;
3. a declaration of the trader of legal significance for the consumer which has not reached him is treated as having reached him, unless it concerns the effectiveness of a declaration sent to the consumer's last notified address where the consumer has not notified the trader of a change of address;
4. a notification or declaration to be made by the consumer to the trader or to a third party must comply with a form stricter than written form or with particular requirements of receipt;
5. the trader is entitled on request to remuneration higher than that fixed at the conclusion of the contract, unless the contract also provides for a reduction in remuneration where the agreed conditions for a change in remuneration are met, the circumstances determining the change are described in the contract and are objectively justified, and the occurrence of the change does not depend on the trader's will.
6. the consumer's right under § 1052 ABGB to withhold his performance until the counter-performance is effected or secured is excluded or restricted where the trader does not perform in accordance with the contract or where performance is endangered by his poor financial circumstances of which the consumer neither knew nor ought to have known at the time of the conclusion of the contract, for example by making the right of retention conditional on the trader acknowledging defects in his performance;
7. a right of retention to which the consumer is entitled by law is excluded or restricted;
8. the consumer's right to discharge his liabilities by set-off is excluded or restricted in the event of the trader's insolvency, or counterclaims which are legally connected with the consumer's liability and which have been judicially established or acknowledged by the trader are excluded or restricted;
9. a duty of the trader to compensate for personal injury is excluded or restricted, or a duty of the trader to compensate for other damage is excluded or restricted where he or a person for whom he is responsible has caused the damage intentionally or by gross negligence;
10. the trader, or a body or person within his sphere of influence, is authorised to decide with binding effect on the consumer whether the services provided to the consumer by the trader conform to the agreement;
11. a burden of proof is imposed on the consumer which he does not bear by law;
12. the consumer's rights to an item taken over by the trader for processing lapse within an unreasonably short period;
13. the interest payable in the event of the consumer's default exceeds the rate of interest agreed for payment in accordance with the contract by more than five percentage points per year;
14. the right to invoke a mistake made by him, or the absence or lapse of the basis of the transaction, is excluded or restricted in advance, for example also by an agreement that statements of the trader do not concern the main subject matter or an essential characteristic of it (§ 871(1) ABGB);
15. after the occurrence of default he undertakes to pay collection or enforcement costs, unless those costs are separately and itemised in the agreement, or insofar as those costs were not necessary for the appropriate collection or enforcement of the claim."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-1-q1 .

lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "08a14972abf4dbbe4c3de4815293dd821aa467bd865aa141a9d063ba65cb2e38" ;
    lgo:text "(3) A contractual provision contained in general terms and conditions or standard contract forms is ineffective if it is worded unclearly or unintelligibly."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-KSCHG-s6-3-q1 .

lg:AT-KSCHG-title-ac92bd9b0018-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "ac92bd9b00185f3e2018f6ec4cf9d7cf31bc443d78e375807b1fcfb958866ea2" ;
    lgo:text "Federal Act of 8 March 1979 laying down provisions for the protection of consumers (Konsumentenschutzgesetz – KSchG)"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-KSCHG .

lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "c676391f66e4f194d452683b9d132d1bd0454286bc8a55afe7425ba0b54ca45d" ;
    lgo:text "(1) The media owner of every periodical medium shall publish the information specified in paragraphs 2 to 4. For periodical media works, the imprint shall also state the web address at which this information can be found easily, directly and permanently, or the information shall be appended to each issue of the medium. For broadcasting programmes, all this information shall either be made permanently available on an easily found teletext page or be published in the Official Gazette of the \"Wiener Zeitung\" within one month of the start of broadcasting and in the first month of each calendar year. On a website, this information shall be made available so that it can be found easily, directly and permanently. For recurring electronic media, either the web address at which this information can be found easily, directly and permanently shall be stated, or the information shall be appended to each issue of the medium. Where the media owner is a service provider within the meaning of § 3 no. 2 ECG, BGBl. I No. 152/2001, the disclosure may be made available together with the information under § 5 ECG."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-1-q1 .

lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "ded360f2b85900ad9d1bf75f786ff69f9fdbbf4e0f66fe617e10e012296c1ea4" ;
    lgo:text "(2) The following shall be stated: the media owner with name or company name, business purpose, place of residence or seat (establishment), and the names of the media owner's representative bodies and, where there is a supervisory board, its members. In addition, for all persons holding a direct or indirect interest in a media owner, their respective ownership, participation, share and voting-right holdings shall be stated. Any silent partnerships in the media owner and in the persons holding a direct or indirect interest in it within the meaning of the preceding sentence shall also be stated, and trust relationships shall be disclosed at every level. Where foundations hold a direct or indirect interest, the founder and the respective beneficiaries of the foundation shall also be disclosed. Where the media owner is an association, or an association holds a direct or indirect interest in the media owner, the association's board and purpose shall be stated. Persons holding a direct or indirect interest, trustors, founders and beneficiaries of a foundation are obliged, at the request of the media owner, to provide it with the information it needs to fulfil its disclosure obligation."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-2-q1 .

lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-4-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "228eecbdc55165239c343351dd7dd0b3176478299b61ea60b08988886f740035" ;
    lgo:text "(4) A statement on the basic direction of a periodical print work (editorial line) or of any other periodical medium shall also be published. Within the meaning of § 2, changes and additions to the basic direction take effect only once they have been published."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-4-q1 .

lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-5-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "a5d616fb4d9b47ab5d49c78aa28142c3b0cac43c3bca17b50c1ff219dc91b136" ;
    lgo:text "(5) For a medium within the meaning of § 1(1) no. 5a(b) and (c) whose information content does not go beyond presenting the media owner's personal life or presenting the media owner, and is not capable of influencing public opinion, only the name or company name, where applicable the business purpose, and the place of residence or seat of the media owner shall be stated. Paragraphs 3 and 4 do not apply to such media."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-MEDIENG-s25-5-q1 .

lg:AT-MEDIENG-title-9fae080ed736-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "9fae080ed7363236b6a9c889dda3f436ec91c3e469d5cef69eb8d4959d7a492c" ;
    lgo:text "Federal Act of 12 June 1981 on the Press and Other Journalistic Media (Media Act – MedienG)"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-11"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-MEDIENG .

lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118-i1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "e49c7b4216405cd9b3580b80c0a5a1e918defa3ee0e7399aa83c319539e5c5a7" ;
    lgo:text "It is correct that § 5(1) no. 3 ECG does not explicitly mention a telephone number. But from the wording chosen by the legislature, \"including its electronic mail address\", it must be derived that besides the latter at least one other individual communication channel (cf. \"get in touch\") must be given, such as telephone or fax (see also Blume/Hammerl aaO 71, Burgstaller/Minichmayr aaO 54 and Zankl aaO 100). Brenn (aaO 208) rightly points out in this context that not every user has an e-mail address or access to one."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118-i1-q1 .

lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118-i2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "18d7cf348735e42f1808449b45866f3d1ff6529112adb881a7285946407e211f" ;
    lgo:text "In the case at hand, the impugned websites first gave an incorrect telephone number, then a telephone number under which no connection to the service provider could be made. Thus, besides the electronic mail address, the giving of another suitable individual communication channel was lacking; nor was it alleged or found that a fax number had been given. The court of appeal was therefore right to hold the defendant liable also for a breach of § 5(1) no. 3 ECG."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118-i2-q1 .

lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118-tenor-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "5dca0c258a8242c48620a54776ca1dc85724d49965e5a1dc338a0638bb5ebd82" ;
    lgo:text "1. The defendant's appeal on points of law is not upheld."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118-tenor-1-q1 .

lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118-title-7989ecae180a-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "7989ecae180adb8815cf4993a03bcb8b1d6276c3c58a863971bc4efbb0bf7138" ;
    lgo:text "Supreme Court, Judgment of 18 November 2003 – 4 Ob 219/03i"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2003-1118 .

lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-i1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "c5e9ca0f229376e89ec8ed0a28ebee6ac9d09e1799519fac678231a72af39479" ;
    lgo:text "Nor is it harmful that the required data (name or corporate name on the one hand, and register number and register court on the other) are not collected in a specially highlighted \"Impressum\" field, provided they are otherwise constantly, easily and directly accessible within the web presence, which is to be examined according to the circumstances of the individual case (here, for example, the company names in the upper right area of the homepage)."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-i1-q1 .

lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-i2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "2579f3c53c836d771837e79b39a7bbabece4660d77c69291e1bf815c38db762f" ;
    lgo:text "These considerations can be summarised as follows: whether a service provider fulfils the disclosure obligations of § 5(1) ECG is, according to the circumstances of the individual case, to be examined as to whether the user can obtain constantly, easily and directly the data necessary to identify the service provider and to enable contact to be made. The use of commonly used abbreviations is no more harmful than the use of individual abbreviations, such as of the name, if the unabridged full wording can be gathered constantly, easily and directly from the overall presentation."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-i2-q1 .

lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-i3-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "027dce03f4b8c2be39aee50a3c33382ef75f4e2a07a249d63ef8d5f034cb2427" ;
    lgo:text "For lack of a proven breach of the disclosure provisions invoked, the claimant's application for an injunction is unfounded."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-i3-q1 .

lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-tenor-1-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "fa26005c3d24e84da5ea0827420e318c830b3da11ea2a062982ac25d07ab2460" ;
    lgo:text "The appeal on points of law is not upheld."@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-tenor-1-q1 .

lg:AT-OGH-2013-1217-title-69c818647605-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "69c81864760503b532549e86922e4c25e3b6da767b825a4fd1ad57462dd7d67b" ;
    lgo:text "Supreme Court, Order of 17 December 2013 – 4 Ob 211/13b"@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "devin" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translatedProperty eli:title ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
